      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The LNP-membrane interaction is predicated upon electrostatic interactions between the positively charged ionizable lipids and the anionic phospholipid headgroups of the target epithelial cell plasma membrane, promoting endocytosis and subsequent endosomal destabilization via proton sponge effects. Upon cytosolic release, the guide RNA (gRNA) undergoes Watson-Crick base pairing with the protospacer adjacent motif (PAM)-proximal target sequence, inducing a conformational shift in the Cas9 nuclease domain. This structural rearrangement activates the HNH and RuvC nuclease domains, enabling sequence-specific double-strand break (DSB) induction proximal to the target site, thereby initiating downstream DNA repair pathways.",
      "source": "target",
